      Cosine and sine have a center of symmetry in the horizontal middle of their period. One side is the opposite of the other.
      So any 2π jump produces equivalent results. Any π jump gets us halfway there, in the horizontally mirrored part of the period.
      So:

        cos (x ± π)  =  -cos (x)    and    sin (x ± π)  =  -sin (x)

