                                                          s'²  +  2 sin (φ_ν) s'  +  1

                                         1                                     ωc²
    <=>    β_ν (s)  =  ------------------------------------  =  ---------------------------------
                        (s/ωc)²  +  2 sin (φ_ν) s/ωc  +  1       s²  +  2 sin (φ_ν) ωc s  +  ωc²


  Now each angle φ_ν will produce a distinct transfer function. B (s) is their product.
  
  Update: N can be odd now.
  How do we deal with this?
  We need an extra 1-pole filter, let's buid it first.

  It has a pole at  s' = -1. So its denominator is:
                  
